)O+_06 Integration parameters  (WARNING: Do not delete this line!!)
) Lines beginning with `)' are ignored.
) Note: densities must be in same unit distance of vertices!
) Author:        Andre Amarante        (A. Amarante)     - andre.amarante@unesp.br
) Last modification: 22/01/2025
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
) Important integration parameters:
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
 number of grid points = 99999
 dump interval = 99999
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
) Integration options:
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
 output precision (low-4, medium-9 or high-15) = high
 use mascons' method = no
 use cubic mascons = no
 use potential from cubic file = no
 x-size = 1.d0
 y-size = 1.d0
 z-size = 1.d0
 read points from grid file = yes
 initial grid point x (distance) = -100
 final grid point x (distance) = -90.5
 initial grid point y (distance) = -100
 final grid point y (distance) = 100
 initial grid point z (distance) = -100
 final grid point z (distance) = 100
 x increment (distance) = 0.5
 y increment (distance) = 0.5
 z increment (distance) = 0.5
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
) These parameters do not need to be adjusted often:
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
 layers' densities (mass_unit/distance_unit^3) List from most superficial to deepest = 0.5d12
 rotation period (hours) = 15.92d0
 factor = 1.0
 a (distance_unit)= 0
 b (distance_unit)= 0
 c (distance_unit)= 0
)---------------------------------------------------------------------
 gravitational constant (distance_unit^3/time_unit^2/mass_unit) = 6.67428d-20
